{"id": "EUVD-2026-100481", "enisaUuid": "5db29669-9bac-3f28-91ec-fd731b05d03a", "description": "The auth0/nextjs-auth0 SDK validates that the returnTo parameter is a same-origin URL. The SDK then stores this value and, in a later step, reconstructs it for the post-authentication redirect. The reconstruction logic can produce a URL that browsers interpret as an absolute or scheme-relative path, leading to a redirect to an unintended domain.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T20:08:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-14T18:41:32", "baseScore": 6.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://trust.okta.com/security-advisories/improper-validation-of-post-login-redirect-url-in-nextjs-auth0-cve-2026-107369", "https://github.com/auth0/nextjs-auth0/security/advisories/GHSA-5vvp-h2v6-59j6"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107369"], "assigner": "Okta", "epss": 0.23, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3ebdded1-8b04-3501-9820-5c2d307354ec", "product": {"name": "nextjs-auth0", "vendor": {"name": "auth0"}}, "product_version": "0 <4.32.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "0294b800-858a-33bb-a3fa-cfebd515a2e2", "vendor": {"name": "auth0"}}], "isExploited": false}